    "function": "Involved in nitrogen metabolism via ammonium assimilation. Catalyzes the ATP-dependent biosynthesis of glutamine from glutamate and ammonia. Also able to use GTP. D-glutamate is a poor substrate, and DL-glutamate shows about 50% of the standard specific activity. Also plays a key role in controlling the ammonia levels within infected host cells and so contributes to the pathogens capacity to inhibit phagosome acidification and phagosome-lysosome fusion. Involved in cell wall biosynthesis via the production of the major component poly-L-glutamine (PLG). PLG synthesis in the cell wall occurs onl",
